⚡️🇨🇦 Federal Ammunition has secured two Canadian government contracts. The Department of National Defence selected Federal's 110-grain Tactical Bonded .300 Blackout rounds for supersonic duty use, with up to 330,000 rounds, and its 108-grain Semi-Jacketed Frangible .300 Blackout for training, with up to 530,000 rounds.

Separately, the Royal Canadian Mounted Police awarded Federal a contract for 51,000 shells of 12-gauge 1-ounce reduced-recoil slugs and 120,250 shells of 12-gauge 00 buckshot, also reduced-recoil. That agreement runs one year, with an optional one-year renewal. Federal previously supplied the RCMP under a similar 12-gauge duty contract.

